  "brief": "EQT to acquire Qiagen for €10.8 billion, while LSEG is acquiring Octus for $3.5 billion, in two of today's major M&A announcements.\n\nEQT / Qiagen (Announced): EQT to Acquire Qiagen. EQT is buying Qiagen for €10.8 billion [1, 2, 3]. The deal was announced on October 21 [6, 7, 8]. No further information is available [4, 5, 7].\nLSEG / Octus (Announced): LSEG to Acquire Octus. LSEG is acquiring Octus for $3.5 billion [11, 12, 13]. The deal is aimed at shielding LSEG from AI disruption [11, 13]. The acquisition was first announced on October 13 [14].\nCircle8 / SThree (Announced): Circle8 and SThree Deal. Circle8 is making a takeover bid for SThree [17, 18]. Circle8 has been granted two extensions to firm up its bid [15, 16]. The deal is still in the early stages [15, 16, 17].\nCencora / American Oncology Network (Announced): Cencora to Acquire American Oncology Network. Cencora is acquiring American Oncology Network in a $2.4 billion deal [19, 20]. The deal has been announced [19, 20]. No further information is available [19, 20].\nBlackstone / Apollo (Announced): Blackstone and Apollo NFL Deal. Blackstone and Apollo are exploring the possibility of buying minority stakes in NFL teams [21, 22]. The deal has not been finalized and is still in the early stages [21, 22].\nPlurilock / Quantum eMotion (Pending approval): Plurilock to Acquire Quantum eMotion. Plurilock is acquiring Quantum eMotion for $24M USD [24]. The deal is pending shareholder approval [23, 24]. Plurilock will vote on the acquisition [23].\nSmith & Wesson / Savage Arms (Announced): Smith & Wesson Acquires Savage Arms. Smith & Wesson is acquiring Savage Arms for $160 million [25]. The deal brings together two historic brands in the firearms industry [25]. The acquisition is the latest move by Smith & Wesson in its efforts to expand its product line [25].\nTechouse / Ambio (Announced): Techouse Acquires Ambio. Techouse is acquiring Ambio, expanding its offshore water treatment business [26]. 